# DataSweep Pro
#
# Everything in this file is baked into the client bundle at build time. Vite
# only exposes variables prefixed VITE_, and anything it exposes is readable by
# anyone who opens the page. So this file holds configuration, never secrets.
#
# There is no server-side variable to set, because there is no server: the app
# is a static bundle and the data never leaves the browser tab. That is also why
# there is no GITHUB_TOKEN here. A token belongs to the person exporting, is
# entered in the export dialog, is held in memory for that tab only, and is gone
# on reload.

# GitHub export mode. Default: demo.
#
#   demo  Assembles the artifacts, hashes them, and shows the full preflight —
#         then stops. No network request is made and the PR number is derived
#         from the manifest hash. This is the default so a deployment that
#         configures nothing cannot make a request it did not intend to.
#
#   live  Enables the token field in the export dialog. The user supplies a
#         fine-grained personal access token scoped to the repositories they
#         choose, which is a tighter permission boundary than any allow-list
#         this app could maintain, and no third party ever holds it.
VITE_GITHUB_EXPORT_MODE=demo
